<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Curicaueri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Curicaueri was the fire and sun god of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/purepecha-empire">Purépecha</a> of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, patron of the ruling Uacúsecha lineage and of the Purépecha state. Priests kept fires burning in his honour on temple platforms, and war was waged to supply him with captives and firewood. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/relacion-de-michoacan">Relación de Michoacán</a> is the main source for his cult.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/curicaueri.jpg" alt="Curicaueri" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Josuemirandazepeda · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Exvoto_para_Curicaueri.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
